  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-14T03:53:30.264Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Seems like a mute toggle keybinding is well over due for a game emphasized on the Social Experience.  I use the original Oculus Rift touch controllers there are two button unused in VRchat. \"Y and B\" have no function.  The few seconds to open the menu and hit the mute button is long enough to derail a conversation.       With the menu there is no reason it needs to be a two handed menu a dead battery in a controller makes it unusable. I get it like holding a futuristic transparent tablet, maybe just an option to make it static?  I guarantee I'm not the only one who thinks this, and these annoyances are not game breaking it'd just be  a nice quality of life update. \n\n--and a thank you to everyone here for everything you do. Keep it up!",
